1
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:03,183
Where is Sofia?

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:05,816
No, no, no! My phone is dead!

3
00:00:10,566 --> 00:00:16,510
Today we are going to the city center. It's my mom's birthday tomorrow. I need a present.

4
00:00:16,710 --> 00:00:18,203
And I need a burger.

5
00:00:18,403 --> 00:00:20,550
Of course you do.

6
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,545
Let's learn how to ask for directions and ask for help.

7
00:00:25,145 --> 00:00:29,814
Okay, Gus. The city is very big. Please stay with me.

8
00:00:30,014 --> 00:00:32,696
Yes, yes. I will stay with you.

9
00:00:32,896 --> 00:00:35,502
Don't go far. Do you understand?

10
00:00:35,702 --> 00:00:39,184
I understand. I'm not a baby. I'm a goose.

11
00:00:39,384 --> 00:00:41,283
That's the problem.

12
00:00:44,383 --> 00:00:48,843
Oh, look! A flower shop. Mom loves flowers.

13
00:00:48,893 --> 00:00:51,522
Wait here, Gus. I'll be back in two minutes.

14
00:00:51,722 --> 00:00:54,122
Okay. Two minutes. No problem.

15
00:00:56,422 --> 00:00:58,601
Hmm... What is that smell?

16
00:00:58,651 --> 00:00:59,590
Burgers!

17
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:02,780
Two for one? Two burgers for one price?

18
00:01:02,830 --> 00:01:05,748
I have to see this. Just for one minute...

19
00:01:11,998 --> 00:01:16,362
Where is the burger place? It was here... I think.

20
00:01:16,412 --> 00:01:20,524
Hmm. This street is different. Where is the flower shop?

21
00:01:20,574 --> 00:01:22,058
Where is Sofia?

22
00:01:22,558 --> 00:01:26,928
Okay. Don't panic, Gus. Take your phone. Call Sofia.

23
00:01:27,528 --> 00:01:30,011
No, no, no! My phone is dead!

24
00:01:30,061 --> 00:01:33,319
I'm lost! I'm a lost goose in a big city!

25
00:01:33,819 --> 00:01:37,489
Okay. Calm down. I can ask someone for help.

26
00:01:37,539 --> 00:01:39,784
People are nice. Probably.

27
00:01:42,834 --> 00:01:45,517
Excuse me. Sorry to bother you.

28
00:01:45,717 --> 00:01:47,837
Yes, dear? Can I help you?

29
00:01:48,037 --> 00:01:51,731
I think I'm lost. I'm looking for a flower shop.

30
00:01:51,931 --> 00:01:57,962
A flower shop? There are many flower shops in this city. What is the name of the street?

31
00:01:58,162 --> 00:02:01,449
I don't know. It's next to a big burger place.

32
00:02:01,649 --> 00:02:04,997
Ah! Big Burger! It's on Green Street.

33
00:02:05,197 --> 00:02:08,064
Yes! That's it! How do I get there?

34
00:02:08,264 --> 00:02:12,490
It's easy. Go straight. Then turn left at the bank.

35
00:02:12,510 --> 00:02:16,289
Then go past the park. Green Street is on your right.

36
00:02:16,489 --> 00:02:21,787
Go straight... turn left at the bank... past the park... on my right.

37
00:02:21,987 --> 00:02:24,945
That's right. It takes about ten minutes.

38
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:26,847
Ten minutes? On foot?

39
00:02:27,047 --> 00:02:30,267
On foot. Or five minutes if you fly.

40
00:02:30,467 --> 00:02:35,312
Ha! I'm a goose, but I don't fly. I walk. Thank you so much!

41
00:02:35,512 --> 00:02:37,828
You're welcome, dear. Good luck!

42
00:02:40,428 --> 00:02:43,544
Okay. The bank. Turn... left? Or right?

43
00:02:43,844 --> 00:02:45,768
Right. Right is right!

44
00:02:54,418 --> 00:02:57,572
Hmm. This is not a park. This is a shop.

45
00:02:57,772 --> 00:02:59,448
Hello! Can I help you?

46
00:02:59,648 --> 00:03:02,521
Yes, please. Do you sell phone chargers?

47
00:03:02,721 --> 00:03:05,831
Sorry, we don't. But we have maps.

48
00:03:06,031 --> 00:03:08,608
A map! Perfect. How much is it?

49
00:03:08,808 --> 00:03:10,274
It's five dollars.

50
00:03:10,474 --> 00:03:14,461
I have... three dollars. And a coupon for burgers.

51
00:03:14,661 --> 00:03:17,187
Sorry, the coupon doesn't work here.

52
00:03:17,387 --> 00:03:18,897
Can I pay by card?

53
00:03:19,097 --> 00:03:20,684
Yes, of course.

54
00:03:20,884 --> 00:03:23,362
Oh no. My card is at home.

55
00:03:23,962 --> 00:03:27,179
Okay... Here's a small map. It's free.

56
00:03:27,379 --> 00:03:30,457
Really? Thank you! You are very kind.

57
00:03:30,657 --> 00:03:32,776
No problem. Where do you want to go?

58
00:03:32,976 --> 00:03:35,524
Green Street. Next to Big Burger.

59
00:03:35,724 --> 00:03:38,733
We are here. Green Street is here.

60
00:03:38,783 --> 00:03:42,866
You went the wrong way. Turn left at the bank, not right.

61
00:03:43,166 --> 00:03:45,585
Left. Of course. I knew that.

62
00:03:46,185 --> 00:03:50,487
Excuse me, can I use your phone? I need to call my friend.

63
00:03:50,687 --> 00:03:52,355
Sure. Here you are.

64
00:03:53,055 --> 00:03:55,743
Hmm... I don't remember her number.

65
00:03:55,793 --> 00:03:59,462
I know the burger menu by heart. But not her number.

66
00:04:06,712 --> 00:04:11,405
Okay, Gus, I'm ready! ...Gus? Gus?

67
00:04:11,455 --> 00:04:14,337
Where is he? I said wait here!

68
00:04:17,037 --> 00:04:19,896
The number you are calling is not available.

69
00:04:20,096 --> 00:04:25,553
Oh no. His phone is dead. Again.

70
00:04:27,253 --> 00:04:32,913
Excuse me, officer! Can you help me, please? I lost my friend.

71
00:04:33,113 --> 00:04:35,838
Of course. What does your friend look like?

72
00:04:36,038 --> 00:04:42,215
He is tall. He is white. He has a long neck and an orange beak.

73
00:04:42,415 --> 00:04:44,892
A long neck and an orange beak?

74
00:04:45,092 --> 00:04:47,182
And he's wearing a blue tie.

75
00:04:47,382 --> 00:04:49,987
Miss... is your friend a goose?

76
00:04:50,187 --> 00:04:52,701
Yes. Is that a problem?

77
00:04:52,901 --> 00:04:55,816
No, no. Where did you see him last?

78
00:04:56,016 --> 00:04:59,558
Here. Next to the flower shop. About twenty minutes ago.

79
00:04:59,758 --> 00:05:02,498
Hmm. Is there a place he loves?

80
00:05:02,698 --> 00:05:05,558
Food. He loves burgers.

81
00:05:05,758 --> 00:05:07,040
Like Big Burger?

82
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:09,883
Of course! Thank you, officer!

83
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:22,704
Go straight... turn left at the bank... past the park... Green Street! I did it!

84
00:05:23,404 --> 00:05:25,784
Gus!

85
00:05:25,984 --> 00:05:26,922
Sofia!

86
00:05:28,222 --> 00:05:31,360
Where were you? I was so worried!

87
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:37,576
I'm sorry. I smelled burgers. Then I got lost. Then my phone died.

88
00:05:37,776 --> 00:05:39,964
I said wait here.

89
00:05:40,164 --> 00:05:47,822
I know. But I learned a lot today. I asked for directions. I went to a shop. I got a free map!

90
00:05:48,022 --> 00:05:52,230
You asked for help in English? I'm proud of you.

91
00:05:52,430 --> 00:05:54,988
Thank you. Now... two for one?

92
00:05:55,188 --> 00:05:58,489
Okay. But this time you stay with me.

93
00:05:58,689 --> 00:06:01,284
I promise. ...After the burgers.

94
00:06:05,384 --> 00:06:09,704
Now it's practice time! Listen and repeat after me. Ready?

95
00:06:10,404 --> 00:06:12,751
Excuse me. Can you help me?

96
00:06:15,851 --> 00:06:18,199
Excuse me. Can you help me?

97
00:06:19,099 --> 00:06:20,547
I think I'm lost.

98
00:06:23,647 --> 00:06:25,095
I think I'm lost.

99
00:06:25,995 --> 00:06:27,716
How do I get to Green Street?

100
00:06:30,816 --> 00:06:32,538
How do I get to Green Street?

101
00:06:33,438 --> 00:06:37,041
Go straight. Turn left. Turn right.

102
00:06:40,141 --> 00:06:43,744
Go straight. Turn left. Turn right.

103
00:06:44,644 --> 00:06:45,928
It's on your right.

104
00:06:49,028 --> 00:06:50,311
It's on your right.

105
00:06:51,211 --> 00:06:52,243
How much is it?

106
00:06:55,343 --> 00:06:56,375
How much is it?

107
00:06:57,275 --> 00:06:58,713
Can I pay by card?

108
00:07:01,813 --> 00:07:03,251
Can I pay by card?

109
00:07:04,151 --> 00:07:06,291
Can I use your phone, please?

110
00:07:09,391 --> 00:07:11,531
Can I use your phone, please?

111
00:07:12,431 --> 00:07:14,128
I lost my friend.

112
00:07:17,228 --> 00:07:18,925
I lost my friend.

113
00:07:19,825 --> 00:07:21,206
What does he look like?

114
00:07:24,306 --> 00:07:25,687
What does he look like?

115
00:07:26,787 --> 00:07:34,349
Quick question! At the bank, Gus turned right. Was that correct? Write your answer in the comments!

116
00:07:38,849 --> 00:07:41,107
No. He needed to turn left.

117
00:07:43,807 --> 00:07:49,139
Great job! Now you can ask for directions, shop, and ask for help in English.

118
00:07:49,339 --> 00:07:50,907
And find burgers.

119
00:07:51,007 --> 00:07:54,187
Subscribe for the next story! Bye!

120
00:07:54,287 --> 00:07:57,141
Bye! ...Wait. Where is the exit?
